@startuml
'=============================================================================
' KIND      MEASURED -- every edge below was extracted from the source.
' GROUNDING the twelve live packages named in PRODUCT.md
'           "What is live code vs research record".
' CHECK     python scripts/check_architecture_grounding.py
'           re-derives these edges and fails on any drift in either
'           direction. Do not add an edge here by hand without the code
'           edge to match, and do not delete one to make the check pass.
'
' Reading note: the live packages do not use package-qualified imports.
' They put sibling directories on sys.path and import bare module names
' (import task_model, import worker as W, import observe). An edge below
' therefore means "some module in A imports a module owned by B", which
' is the dependency that actually constrains change.
'
' A --> B reads "A depends on B".
'=============================================================================
!theme plain
title Learning Lab — live package dependencies (MEASURED)

component "adapters" as adapters
component "inspector" as inspector
component "taskmodel" as taskmodel
component "modeller" as modeller
component "worker" as worker
component "fleet" as fleet
component "supervisor" as supervisor
component "reservation" as reservation
component "enrichment" as enrichment
component "aggregation" as aggregation
component "reconciliation" as reconciliation
component "calendar_job" as calendar_job

' --- task families depend on the shared model contract ------------------
aggregation --> taskmodel : task_model
enrichment --> taskmodel : task_model
reconciliation --> taskmodel : task_model
reservation --> taskmodel : task_model

' --- the modeller composes the families ---------------------------------
modeller --> taskmodel : task_model
modeller --> inspector : observe
modeller --> aggregation : aggregation_model, execute_aggregation
modeller --> enrichment : enrichment_model, execute_enrichment
modeller --> reconciliation : reconciliation_model, execute_reconciliation
modeller --> reservation : reservation_model, execute_reservation

' --- the deterministic runtime ------------------------------------------
worker --> taskmodel : task_model
worker --> inspector : observe
worker --> modeller : builder
worker --> reservation : reservation_model, execute_reservation
calendar_job --> taskmodel : task_model
calendar_job --> reservation : reservation_model, execute_reservation

' --- fleet owns established state and reaches down to the runtime --------
fleet --> worker : worker, runtime
fleet --> modeller : builder, manifest, pipeline
fleet --> adapters : adapters.xlsx

' --- the supervisor reads the fleet and drives the DEFINE glue -----------
supervisor --> fleet : fleet, inbox, confirmations, system_map, map_component
supervisor --> modeller : pipeline
supervisor --> adapters : xlsx

note as N1
**What the measured shape says**

* `taskmodel` and `inspector` are leaves. Nothing they import is live
  product code, so they are the two packages a change can start from
  without pulling anything else with it.
* `modeller` is not only the DEFINE surface: it is the composition
  point for all four task families, and both `worker` and `fleet`
  depend on it. It is the most load-bearing live package, not a UI.
* `calendar_job` reaches the reservation family and the task model
  directly. It does not go through `worker`.
* `fleet -> worker -> modeller -> families -> taskmodel` is the real
  spine. The intended flow view draws several of these arrows the
  other way round, correctly, because flow is not dependency.
* Workbook ingestion enters through `fleet` and `supervisor`, not
  through `modeller` -- see discrepancy register D6.
end note
@enduml
